 ## Pure core — no context, no framework glue
 **Date:** 23. 06. 26
@@ -99,3 +100,10 @@
 **Decision:** The tier-1 member is **`xl2`** in both positions — `.xl2({…})` and `{ xl2: {…} }` — emitting the `2xl:` prefix. The generic `.variant("2xl", {…})` form (whose `TailwindBreakpoint` union already contains `"2xl"`) remains the exact-spelling route, as it is for every other variant. Container-query breakpoints (`@sm`, `@max-lg`, …) stay `.variant()`-only.
 **Reasoning:** A quoted `"2xl"` key would be the only quoted member of the whole surface — visually inconsistent, easy for an LLM to mis-emit unquoted (a compile error, but a needless one), and unusable as a method name, splitting the spelling across positions (`.variant("2xl")` but `md: { "2xl": … }`). `xl2` is one uniform identifier in both positions, keeps the breakpoint family prefix-sortable (`sm md lg xl xl2`), and lands in the already-documented "where names diverge from raw Tailwind" divergence family (compound-prefix boundary, `.neg()`, translate axis). Divergence cost is low: `2xl` is rare, and the generic form preserves the trained spelling.
 **Consequences:** `DIRECT_VARIANTS` maps `xl2 → "2xl"`; docs teach `xl2` in the tier-1 table and note the divergence in FLUENT-STYLING's divergence section; the ESLint derived tables treat `xl2` as the owner of the `2xl:` prefix.
+
+## Components live in the app's `src/shared/ui`; `@jtdigital/ui` retired
+**Date:** 01. 10. 26
+**Context:** The instruction-set decision (23. 06. 26) named `@jtdigital/ui` as the user-land home. That package (`projects-template/packages/ui`) had 0 consumers in 58 repos and 36 lint errors, and as a dependency its classes miss the app safelist. Every app carries `src/shared/ui`, seeded by the template.
+**Decision:** User-land components live in the app's `src/shared/ui`; the template seeds it. `packages/ui` is deleted. The instruction-set test is unchanged.
+**Reasoning:** One component layer, the one apps import, inside the `src/**/*.ts` safelist glob. v8.2.0 RFC-C-04.
+**Consequences:** "Cut to user-land" rulings (L-411, L-188, L-190, L-236, L-238) point at `src/shared/ui`. No package names a design system.
